  "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3{x}^{4}$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+3{x}^{4}} & =\\frac{1}{1-(-3{x}^{4})} \\\\  & =1+(-3{x}^{4})+{(-3{x}^{4})}^{2}+{(-3{x}^{4})}^{3}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-3{x}^{4}+9{x}^{8}-27{x}^{12}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
